Ah. Flummoxed myself yet again with Yankee slang. Monday morning
quarterbacking is like 20-20 hindsight. The derivation of the
expression is as follows...

Many of the major American football games are played on Sunday
afternoon. Football fanatics then discuss the game at work on Monday
morning. Since the fanatics are full of "shoulda woulda coulda" advice
for the team strategist (known as a quarterback) of their favored team,
the practice of post-morteming a game is called...

Monday Morning Quarterbacking.

Quarterbacks abound in the trade press, too!



