Ketil Z Malde  <ketil@ii.uib.no> wrote:
>hobbs@steven.zko.dec.com (Steven Hobbs) writes:
>
>> SPECint depends (mostly but definitely not entirely) on the performance
>> 	of the integer execution core and the first level cache. 
>
>L2, surely?  I thought the footprint was on the order of a megabyte,
>most chips tend to have 32-96K L1, but adequate L2.

SPECint95 performance varies with L2 cache size up until about
0.5 MB, above which the performance is about constant.

SPECint95 is weakly sensitive to L2 performance.  On Pentium II/III
and MIPS R10K, varying the secondary cache speed from 2:1 to 1:1 
results in a change in SPECint95 of 5%-8%.

I suppose one would have to resort to simulation to find out how
performance varies with changes in the L1 cache characteristics.
