In article <7fvnkb$je4$1@nnrp1.dejanews.com>, jamescbilling@my-dejanews.com wrote:
>It is something like:
>
>BACKUP MUA0:VMS055.% /SAVE DUA0: /LOG
>

BACKUP/LIST MUA0:*.* should list the tape for you. If you are trying to 
do a fresh install of OpenVMS V5.5-2 from tape you need something like:

        BACKUP/IMAGE/VERIFY/REWIND MUA0:VMS055.B DUA0:

(I suspect that the name is more likely to be VMS055U2 or some such but I 
don't have that particular install kit hanging around here; replace the 
VMS055 above with whatever you see from a /LIST - remember you want the B 
saveset).

This restores the B saveset, which is an image backup of a minimal disk which 
is bootable and will complete the installation when booted.

The /VERIFY goes back and checks that it really did write the disk properly. I 
wouldn't bother with the /LOG unless you really like voluminous output 
(you'll get error messages anyway and they'll be much easier to see without 
the noise).

The /REWIND rewinds the tape before starting (in case you have done a /LIST to 
see what is on the tape).

