lmbench's main problem is that it often doesn't accurately measure what
it thinks it does.  Aaron Brown and other in Margo Seltzer's group at
Harvard reworked lmbench to eliminate some of the problems and generally
increase accuracy of measurement, producing HBench-OS.  There are papers
on that, as well as source code, which you should be able to find from
Aaron's or Margo's page on eecs.harvard.edu.

