Hi,

Darren <n9807471@scholar.nepean.uws.edu.au> wrote:
: I recently acquired a DECStation 5000/20 from my Uni with OpenBSD 2.4
: installed on it. I would like to find out some info about the hardware,
: like the type of SCSI controller, the network interface, harddrive, etc.
: Does anyone know of a site that would have some/all of this info?

Some DECstation information can be found on NetBSD's pmax port pages
(http://www.netbsd.org/Ports/pmax/) but nothing specific to the 5000/20 
(aka "Maxine"). What might be of interest to you is the Maxine maintenance
manual (http://decstation.unix-ag.org/docs/dec_docs/maxine.ps.gz).

The SCSI controller is a NCR53C94, ethernet is controlled by a LANCE chip
(AMD7990), the hard disk is usually a RZ25 - in the non-DEC world probably
better known as Quantum PD425S.

regards,
