In article <3MET2.2796$Hh5.17@news-reader.bt.net>, "Jonathan McCormack" <McCormackJ@BelfastCity.Gov.UK> writes:
:I was wondering if it's possible to send/get Internet E-mail using VMS Mail.
:I can do it with OpenVMS Netscape quite easily but we also have users with
:dumb terminals out there who could do with it.

  Ayup.  It's possible.  Works just fine, too.  You probably even have it
  as part of your installation of the IP package your Netscape mail package 
  is already using as a transport.

  Once you have SMTP configured -- given that you are using Netscape mail, 
  this is probably already done -- simply enter the IP address at the MAIL 
  SEND command To: or CC: prompt.

  I'd suggest a tour through the OpenVMS User's Guide, as it covers this
  and a variety of other topics.  For IP questions, take a look at the
  documentation for the particular IP package installed -- for the TCP/IP 
  Services IP package, versions V4.2 or the current V5.0 are probably the
  most common versions found on OpenVMS V7.1 systems.

