Burning a decstation-bootable CD is awkward. Ultrix ships with a
512-byte-sectored image of an FFS filesystem and standard scsi-disk
bootblocks. Emulating that, with a NetBSD kernel and filesystem on the
CD image, is known to work.


|> Now I've tried to make a new SCSI diskimage onto a linux (2.2.5 kernel).
|> So I've created a netbsd partition (fs and swap) (must have 512k
