|> disk (no errors returned).

If this is a NetBSD disk image... trying to create `partitions' for a
BSD filesystem and swap under (i386) Linux won't work.
I think you should instead be doing something like:

	gunzip -c > diskimage.gz | dd of=/dev/sdd bs=10240

to put the diskimage onto the raw disk, overwriting what an i386
kernel thinks is the MBR label area (and bypassing any MBR partitioning).
I dont know about installing Linux, sorry.



