> down the Celeron's L2 cache artificially?

  No, actually quite the opposite.  According to MDR the Mendocino
  Celeron critical word L2 latency is 8 clocks compared to 14 for
  Xeon and 18 for Pentium II.  In contrast the XP1000 L2 uses
  conventional 166 MHz synchronous burst SRAMs which give a load
  to use latency of 14 clocks.  The lmbench results are rather
  puzzling since 14 * 2 ns is distinctly longer than 8 * 2.2 ns.

