Despite the revisionist history that you and Jonathan may be
trying to apply, the 11/70 was the first PDP-11 with 22-bit
addressing and a 22-bit Unibus to memory map.  The 11/44,
11/84, and 11/94 are also DEC PDP-11 hardware implementations
with 22-bit memory management and available 22-bit Unibus to memory
maps.  There are also several third-party implementations of
22-bit memory addressing to Unibus maps.  All of these are well-
supported by the PDP-11 OS's.

