I've seen this too.  And it's not trivial to tell the difference
between the CPU being the limiter and the memory bus/interconnect
bandwidth being the limiter.  I haven't seen machines that offer good
statistics about bus utilization.  Most CPUs now have performance
counters that let you deduce average cycles per instruction, cycles per
load/store, cache misses, etc. which can indirectly give you a feel
about bus utilization but it'd be nice if chipsets would give us some
