Jason Brady wrote:

> Jeeze!  This is very perplexing.  By all accounts it should
> work.  I checked the console connection, cable, settings,
> TU-85 connectors, power cables, etc. again.  Still getting
> a string of "@" characters.  One thing I noticed, when an
> RS-232 line status monitor is hooked up to the terminal alone,
> pin 2 is green (negative voltage - transmits on 2, receives on
> 3, DTE). When the VAX console is connected, the LED is dark.
> The garbage characters cause the pin 3 red LED to flicker,
> but no activity is apparent when typing characters on the
> terminal (pin 2 red LED should flash).  All the LEDs are dark
> when the RS-232 line monitor is attached to the console cable
> alone.  Did a continuity test on the CPU to the console connector
> cable & null modem cable -- both OK.  Do you think this points to
> the driver and/or receiver chips on the RDM?
I don't think so, because you tested the machine with the RDM removed
and the cables swapped over to the non-RDM positions, and got the same
results. Are you sure that the console cable is on the correct set of
backplane pins? Are you sure that the RS232 cable you're using between
the terminal and the backpanel console connector is wired right? I got
a cable with my machine, and so didn't have to bother about this, but
I assume that a standard null-modem cable, swapping 2 and 3, should do
fine. You've tried swapping the L0004, haven't you? That eliminates the
console line uart as the source of the problem. 

You said that you can see activity on the RS232 monitor when the console
terminal is connected to the monitor. The fact that the monitor shows no
activity when attached to the cable, with the vax on the other end of
the
cable, suggests strongly that either (a) the RS232 line interface chips
on
the vax are shot or (b) the backplane connector is on the wrong set of
pins,
or (c) the terminal cable is wired wrong. 
I think we can probably eliminate (a), which leaves (b) and (c).

Can you attach the monitor directly to the console connector on the vax
(or failing directly, via a 25-way straight-through cable)?

James



