Jason Brady wrote:
> Jeeze!  This is very perplexing.  By all accounts it should
> work.  I checked the console connection, cable, settings,
> TU-85 connectors, power cables, etc. again.  Still getting
> a string of "@" characters.  One thing I noticed, when an
> RS-232 line status monitor is hooked up to the terminal alone,
> pin 2 is green (negative voltage - transmits on 2, receives on
> 3, DTE). When the VAX console is connected, the LED is dark.
> The garbage characters cause the pin 3 red LED to flicker,
> but no activity is apparent when typing characters on the
> terminal (pin 2 red LED should flash).  All the LEDs are dark
> when the RS-232 line monitor is attached to the console cable
> alone.  Did a continuity test on the CPU to the console connector
> cable & null modem cable -- both OK.  Do you think this points to
> the driver and/or receiver chips on the RDM?

When the status monitor is plugged into the terminal cable you
get green on 2. When it is plugged into the VAX (WITHOUT the
terminal cable being connected), you should get green on 3.

If you get green on 2, then you shouldn't be using a null modem
cable (or you could use 2 null modem cables in a row).

If you don't get green on either one, then your connector on
the back of the VAX is wired wrong.



