Compaq/Tandem has announced that they will be transitioning NonStop-UX
users to a "hardened version of Tru 64" shortly after EV7 arrives;  
currently they are based on the MIPS 10000 and looking to go MIPS 12000.

Stratus is doing full fault-tolerance with its Continuum line: PA-RISC
chips and HP-UX (as well as its own VOS and FTX operating systems).
Presumably they're going to be offering the same HP-UX based solution with
some version of Merced. They'd given up on the idea of porting VOS & FTX
over by themselves and Hewlett-Packard's extension of the PA-RISC lifespan
helps keep their users in the fold.

I know that there are a few Sun vendors claiming to offer fault tolerant
UltraSPARC systems with Solaris, but I don't know if its precisely the
same form of fault tolerance. Do the UltraSPARC or Hal's SPARC64GP support
processor lockstepping?

