jeffreyb@gwis2.circ.gwu.edu (Jeffrey Keith Boulier) writes:

>Stratus is doing full fault-tolerance with its Continuum line: PA-RISC
>chips and HP-UX (as well as its own VOS and FTX operating systems).
>Presumably they're going to be offering the same HP-UX based solution with
>some version of Merced. They'd given up on the idea of porting VOS & FTX
>over by themselves and Hewlett-Packard's extension of the PA-RISC lifespan
>helps keep their users in the fold.


The PA-8600 adds a hardware lockstep feature, presumably for HP's next
generation of high end systems (I've heard talk about them, but nothing
concrete beyond hot swap everything, dynamic domains, etc.)

So the fault tolerant HP-UX systems will probably arrive before HP-UX
on IA-64; or at least be available on PA-RISC hardware for a while to
give people a choice of whether to use PA-RISC or IA-64 for some time
for their fault tolerant needs.

