If you compare with the Celeron, you should take a look at the 21164PC
systems.  Half a year ago, I upgraded my system, and at that time the
533MHZ 21164PCs were quite competetive: SX Mainbaord+CPU+1MB L2 Cache
for ATS 6000 (< USD 500); The Celeron 333 appeared at around that time
and together with a motherboard cost a little less money (but often
more time due to BIOS problems); the Celeron 333 probably is a little
slower on average, so the price/performance should be about equal. Or
we could compare with the Pentium-II-350, which at the time cost about
the same as the SX mainboard/CPU combo.

Hmm, looking at the dealer's homepage, they no longer seem to offer
the SX.  Another Austrian dealer appears to offer it, but does not
quote prices on the WWW.

>  And you have to put up with less
