> 	Performance?  I suspect newer Alpha hardware will help counteract
> 	some of NT's sluggishness.. should help a good deal anyhow.

On an absolute scale yes, fast hardware runs WindowsNT faster than
slow hardware. However my experience is that for any given machine, NT
always feels sluggish at some tasks compared to other operating
systems you can run on the same machine. There are architectural and
implementation reasons why NT is sometimes slow and these don't change
with clock speed. If there are some bad algorithms and data structures
in there (a reasonable assumption) a 2X increase in cpu power might
not help - I remember the story of a TRS-80 that outperformed a Cray
beyond a certain dataset size when the Cray was crippled with a
quadratic version of the algorithm.

