2 ns would be pretty fast just to drive a signal from the I/O
drivers of one chip to the I/O drivers in an adjacent chip on
the same printed circuit board.  There is no way that you could
actually drive useful information from the compute circuitry of
one chip to the compute circuitry of another chip with this sort
of latency.  

Bandwidth is another issue, of course.  Communications can be 
pipelined and run at 500 MHz (assuming point-to-point links).
Attenuation may be a problem in printed circuit boards, but
we run 400 MHz signals on cables up to 5 meters in the Origin2000.
