This is, I believe, exactly what most (all?) os's which support the
feature do, it really reminds me of 1983-vintage Expanded Memory Manager
boards on the 8088, mapping small pages (16K?) into a little window
(64K?) which resided somewhere above the crt frame buffer.

It was an abomination then, and it still is so today. The only possible
excuse is that it can actually make some code run faster than without
it. :-)

