I just upgraded the firmware on my AS200 to as200_v6_9.exe.  I obtained it
from the following location on DEC's FTP site:

ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/v5.3/alpha200/

To use it simply format a floppy using DOS on a PC, download as200_v6_9.exe to
the floppy as fwupdate.exe and put it in the Alpha's floppy drive.  Boot the
Alpha to ARC, select Supplemental Menu, then Firmware Update.  Follow the
messages that come up on the display.  I selected the option for Full ROM
Update.

I had been having a problem with this because as soon as the floppy loaded
the screen when solid blue then black with a blinking cursor in the upper
left hand corner.  I pulled out the ATI All-In-Wonder Pro that I had
installed and reinstalled the Number Nine card that shipped with the Alpha. 
That fixed the display problem and I was able to perform the update.

Hope this helps.

Dennis Connolly

