X-Deja-AN: 467178110
References: <7f1ifd$89k$1@nuscc.nus.edu.sg> <7f6kbf$61t$1@nuscc.nus.edu.sg>
Organization: The University of Calgary
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec

Wong Yeow Whye (cscwyw@leonis.nus.edu.sg) wrote:
: Wong Yeow Whye (cscwyw@leonis.nus.edu.sg) wrote:
: : Does anyone know how DU (or should I call it True64 ?) assign those rz
: : numbers for SCSI disks? (them man pages for rz did not help.)
: :
: :

: Thanks for all your replies. I think I have more or less figured it out as
: follows:
: 	if narrow chain and pseudo chain (i.e. IDE devices) are both empty
: 	then
: 		treat wide chain as chain 0
: 	else
: 		treat wide chain as chain 2

This is not quite right. The numbers assigned to SCSI chains are determined
by the contents of the kernel configuration file. Take a look at the
/sys/conf/HOST_NAME_IN_CAPS, and you will see one or more entries of the
kind:

controller      scsi0      at ...
controller      scsi1      at ...

These entries determine the exact location of each SCSI (or SCSI-on-IDE)
controller; by reassigning the numbers appearing in scsi?? you can change
the controller number and hence the rzXY number assigned to the SCSI
devices. This may come quite handy if you have several SCSI controllers
in a single box, and have to physically reshuffle them whithout disturbing
the software configuration.

Regards,

/Serge.P




