In article <19990416103003.19278.00001341@ng19.aol.com>, byerra@aol.com (ByerRA) writes:

  OpenVMS questions are best asked in comp.os.vms.

:Is there any plans to release code to allow OpenVMS v7.1-H2 to boot/run on
:Multia?

  Well -- as there is no such release as "v7.1-H2" -- technically the 
  answer to the question is "no". :-)  The closest releases to this would 
  be V7.1-1H2, a hardware release, and V7.1-2, a maintenance release.  

  There exists a kit of individual files for Multia systems for OpenVMS 
  Alpha V6.2-1H3, and integrated bootstrap kits for V7.1-2 and V7.2.

  I would not expect to see Multia files for any releases prior to V7.2 
  -- other than those already available, of course -- and there is no 
  committment to release Multia kits or bootstrap capabilities for any 
  OpenVMS versions after V7.2.

  Release of a kit for the V7.1-1H2 hardware release would require the 
  development and debugging work needed for the target OpenVMS release, 
  as well as a different (older) installation and bootstrap mechanism 
  or the release of a collection of individual files than that used on 
  OpenVMS Alpha V7.1-2 and later.  (V7.1-1H2 had a one-shot mechanism
  based on VMSINSTAL for bootstrapping unrecognized hardware -- this
  mechanism was moved to PCSI-based kits as part of V7.1-2 and later.)

  Personally, I would move to OpenVMS Alpha V7.1-2 or V7.2, and I would
  discourage any new upgrades to the V7.1-1H1 and V7.1-1H2 releases.

  NB: the files involved in these kits are highly version-dependent.
  They cannot be relocated to other versions and be expected to operate.

 -------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
 Hoff (Stephen) Hoffman   OpenVMS Engineering   hoffman#xdelta.zko.dec.com




