I'm not sure what your point here is. 
The vast majority of us are continually making calls into the OS and the
standard OSs (UNIX/Win/Mac) generally return that something went wrong
with an error code (of course there are always the oddball functions that
behave differently). Certainly within ONE'S OWN functions, one wants to
put ASSERT()s at the entry into the function, but one has little control
over what the OS is doing.

>I guess your way allows you to decide what is an error condition
