I tested the Maxtor disk with dd and got the following results:

# time dd if=/dev/zero of=test bs=1024k count=500
500+0 records in
500+0 records out
0.018u 76.900s 1:17.98 98.6% 0+11k 0+64137io 0pf+0w

# time dd if=test of=/dev/null bs=1024k
500+0 records in
500+0 records out
0.009u 165.087s 3:24.71 80.6% 0+11k 62569+2io 8pf+0w

So it looks like the drive for the CMD646 is not using any kind
of DMA transfer. We will have to buy the 36Gb SCSI disk.

BTW, does somebody know why writing a 500MB file to disk is
double as fast as reading the same file back?

dirk



