>How tough will it be to pull the old motherboard and install a new one?

Having done so many times, it's a pain but doable.  However the
motherboard (and riser board) are really most of the value of the
system, everything else is largely PC components and the box.

To replace the motherboard you'll have to remove /unplug *everything*
and unscrew the MB by several screws attaching it to the bottom.

Why do you think the MB is bad?  If it went "bad" while flashing, see
other notes about the "fail-safe" jumper.

