Kay,

Sounds like the IRS form is a bitmap, which cosumes the memory in the
printer until it runs out.

My rule of thumb with HP LaserJet and workalikes (like the 1152) is to
set up the printer with the maximum memory possible.  It's worth the
investment.  These printers are reliable, many still chugging along
after printing a million or more pages.

I've maxed out the memory on my LaserJets and never have a problem
printing.

One last thing... Excel 95/97/2000 or Excel whatever has absolutely
the WORST prining algorithms.  I upgraded a client from Win 3.1 and
the older Excel Office 4.2 to the new stuff and the printer kept
having out of memory conditions when printing the same old
spreadsheets that printed perfectly with Win 3.1/Excel... Ben Myers

