In article <3713BAD1.774C0D9D@tfn.com>,
	George Milner <george.milner@tfn.com> writes:

> I have a cpio tape archived on DDS2 DAT Tape, was made on a DEC Unix
> server, fairly recent OS (last 6mos) The person who archived the tape
> didn't remember the switches used on the command line.  I need to get
> the data off this tape using cpio on a SGI IRIX 6.5.3 machine w/DAT.
> Does anyone know of the syntax used using cpio and whether there needs
> to be some sort of filter thru DD or whatever.  This is important data
> from a corporate DB and we need some direction!  Appreciate any
> responses

IIRC, IRIX cpio will make suggestions on different options if errors
are detected.  Try various combinations of

 cpio -ivd[c{H [{odc}{crc}6][bBmsS] < /dev/rmt/tpsCdI[{ns}sv]

"ns" is no-swap tape device, and "s" is swap (i.e. swap the bytes as
you read them).

"man cpio" for what all the cpio options mean, and their usage.

Richard Masoner
Champaign Illinois USA



