MOP daemon that the NetBSD/VAX guys wrote(it's available precomplied for
Linux and NetBSD, if I recall correctly).  You'll also need RARP and TFTP,
as usual with netbooting.

    Now, mind you, I know nothing about VMS, and am new to the VAX world as
well, so it might be entirely impossible to do netboot VMS without some odd
work.  I'm not sure if there are boot images available to you in the
distribution.

-

