jamescbilling@my-dejanews.com wrote:
> 
> Thanks to everyone for the help with the TK50 problem, I have opened up the
> machine and there is no TK50 controller :-(.
> 
> The VAXstation 3200 has the model number AA12131 VS31V-D3 and has a
> RD54 attached.
> 
> It did have the following cards inside:
> 2 x M7621-AH        8 Mb RAM
> 1 x M9047               Grant continuity (what the hell is this, is it used in
> clustering?)

Just "filler" boards.  Used in this case to keep the third slot
-the last slot with CD bus on it - empty.

> 1 x M7555               RQDX3 Floppy and Disk controller
> 1 x M7189 - I think  (3 boards) Don't know what these are!

I think you have a M7168 and two M7169's here, the VCB02
video module.

> Then the system performs its tests and stops at ..04..03.. and responds that
> tests are
> complete.

And it passed them succesfully.

> I then get the three chevrons >>>
> 
> If I type SHOW DEVICE or SHOW DEV, the box responds with a ?22 ILL
> CMD.
> 
> If I type HELP, the box responds with a ?2B HLTED.
> 
> If I type SHOW BOOT, the box responds with nothing.

Yep - the KA630 firmware knows none of the above commands.

> If I type BOOT, the screen shimmers and the following appears:
> 
>    2..
>    -DUA0
>    -XQA0
> 
> And then hangs.

This is the sniffer boot order.  The XQA0 is it waiting to
be loaded over the Ethernet.

> I have also tried BOOT DUA0, which results in:
> 
>    2..
>    -DUA0
>    ?42 NOSUCHFILE, DUA0
>    ?06 HLT INST
>    PC = 0000101A
>    Failure.
>    >>>
> 
> BOOT DUA0: also gives the same response.

This means that your DUA0 is formatted, but has no operating
system installed.

Tim.



