At 7 Apr 1999 23:43:16 GMT Keir Spilka
(knspilka@undergrad.math.uwaterloo.ca) wrote:
> Well, I went by the university's surplus sale today and picked
> up this beast for $35 with monitor...great deal...Just one problem
> no one at the school remembers the password, and the machine autoboots

Press ctrl-c just before or while the machine is loading the image,
you'll be left in console mode, type `printenv` and then do a
boot 'bootcommand without -a', the -a is there for boooting the machine
in multi-user. It this doesn't help go for some doc-shopping at
http://www.netbsd.org/ and http://decstation.unix-ag.org/. For example
the "Hardware Maintenance Guide" available at decstation contains all the
available commands and what to do when you get a restricted prompt for a
DECstation 5000/xx, which is very usable for a 1xx (xx being 20, 25 or
30).


