The connector your second power cable is plugged into is just a parking
place for unused cables.  Just unplug it from there, and connect it to your
TK50.

: Second question:  I have been given the TK50, but no cable.  What cable do I
: need to connect a TK50 internally to the controller.  Also which controller
: do I attach it to: J6 Removable Disk 1&2 or J5 Fixed Disk 1?

The TK50 connects directly to a card in the backplane via a ribbon cable.  I
do not offhand remember the Mxxxx number of the TQK50 (controller), but I
am sure someone will be along shortly with that.

: Third question:  I believe that this machine is unable to use SCSI, if I
: purchase a hobbyist CD from DECUS, how I am going to get it onto TK50?  Does
: anyone supply hobbyist VMS on TK50?

There are SCSI host adapters available.  Expect to pay $500 to $2000 for one
though.

: Forth and final question:  I take it that the machine has had the OS removed
: as I cannot boot, I have tried BOOT and BOOT DUA0: and neither work.  I know
: nothing about VMS and come from a HP-UX background.  Does anyone know of a
: good VAX resource (either on-line or printed) that I can get to get me going?

You may have a blank disk, or a dead one.

Go to http://www.altavista.com and search for MicroVAX and FAQ.  You will
find a ton of info.  Also use http://www.dejanews.com to search current and
past postings from related newsgroups.  VAX hobbyists have been asking these
same questions for years.

Jeff.
