Todd Little wrote:
> 
> I'm trying to locate the switch settings for a Digital Personal
> Workstation 200i.  In particular, the clock multiplier settings
> as controlled by switches 2,3,4 of switch pack 1.  The silk
> screen on the motherboard says one thing, and the manual
> says another.  Any ideas which is correct?
> 
> Thanks,
> Todd

If you have the August 96 handbook supplied with the 200i (Appendix A),
then it is probably wrong. The later (updated) handbook available on the
Web site in PDF reverses the setting descriptions. I can mail you this
if you like.

Sw1 1 is the bus speed selector 66MHz = on, 60 = off)

    2,3,4 are the processor speed selectors, based on the bus speed.

2x = 2-on 3-on 4-on
2.5x = 2-off 3-on 4-on
3x = 2-on 3-off 4-on
3.5x = 2-off 3-off 4-on
4x = 2-on 3-on 4-off

If you are thinking of clocking your box, then please make sure your
fans  are running OK!

