  Replacement manual?  Do you mean a service manual, or are you looking
  for a compatible (working) monitor that you can use to replace this 
  (failed?) monitor, or are you looking to use this monitor on a PC.
  If the lattermost, please see the OpenVMS Frequently Asked Questions
  (FAQ) section on using old DIGITAL iron on PC systems.  The OpenVMS 
  FAQ is available via a link at http://www.openvms.digital.com/)

  The usual DIGITAL part number is 2-5-2, or 5-2 characters, and DIGITAL 
  video monitor part numbers typically start with "VR".  Based on the 
  GDM-1961 text, This is probably a VRT19 monitor.  There should be a
  sticker with a serial number and a part number and various related
  information, usually located on the back near the power connection.

  What are you looking for, and what is the host graphics controller that
  you want to use this or the replacement monitor with?  (And please also
  consider using a subject string relevent to the question -- most everybody 
  posting a question here is seeking help.  You want a subject line that
  will attract the attention of somebody that might know the answer to the 
  specific question.)

