Newer Alpha based systems have a Alpha BIOS X86 code emulator in the SRM
and the ARC/AlphaBIOS which will detect and run x86 BIOS code extensions
on options such as Video Cards and SCSI Cards in order to intialize them.

Older Alpha systems do not have this emulator and thus options such as
Video and SCSI require specific Alpha Init code in the SRM and ARC to make
them work.

What's wrong with the internal Video on the Multia, it's fairly good
performance when you load the native drivers?

