In article <370A7492.41C67EA6@dial.pipex.com>,
Chris  <icq@dial.pipex.com> wrote:
>Was a unibus adapter available for this machine ? - would simplify the
>problem considerably since you could then run an emulex or SI controller
>with SMD drives.

Unfortunately not -- KS10s have a UBA (actually they normally have two
of them), but it uses the PA and PB signals for extra data bits instead of
parity error indicators, and runs the disks and tapes in 18-bit mode.
Which, AFAIK, is supported by *none* of the aftermarket controllers.

