Exact syntax is SYSBOOT> set /startup=startup.min.
This prevents any layered product to be started at boot time, so, no
network, no network loop error.

Then, if everything looks fine, log in under the SYSTEM account, disable
the SET NOVERIFY feature (depends on the version of OpenVMS you have.
There is, starting with 7.1 I think, a SYSBOOT param (P2?) which eanbles
boot login), then do a SET VERIFY and a @sys$manager:systartup_V5.com and
watch out any errors (again, the systartup.com procedure name depends on
the version of VMS).

Hopzatelps.

D. aka PRSTSC::DTL



