> been able to figure out.  It looks like this:
> 
> {root}~: netstat -r
>  no namelist
> 
Andrew Gaylard wrote:
>
> So I can't get a routing table from Unix (or anything else for that
> matter:
> 
> {root}~: netstat -i
>  no namelist
 
The problem is that your /sbin/kloadsrv daemon isn't running.
It can be restarted with 

	/sbin/kloadsrv < /dev/console > /dev/console 2>&1

That syntax exists in the /etc/inittab file, in case you forget it.

The real question is why did /sbin/kloadsrv crash?  You don't
mention what release you're running.  There was a
known problem in /vmunix that was causing kloadsrv to randomly
crash.  That problem was fixed as of the V4.0E release and is
fixed in the support/patch releases for V4.0A -> V4.0D.

Joe Mario
Compaq Tru64 Development Environment



