Newsgroups: comp.os.vms,comp.sys.dec

For several reasons, I would like to have a serial terminal as the 
console on my ALPHAstation 255/233.  I have enough terminals and cables.

Some questions.

Why is switching between the graphics and a serial terminal done with 
the SET CONSOLE command?  I mean, suppose the console itself has a 
hardware problem: how can one change it?  Seems to me the S3 switch was 
a better idea.

Does it matter which serial port is used?  Should it be TTA0: or OPA0:?

Obviously, this is something where detailed experimentation is costly. 
I've never been able to see on the serial console all the stuff I see 
when using the graphics console (i.e. output from SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM and 
so on).  Is there a way to do this?  A related question is is it 
possible to have the output go to both the console and STARTUP.LOG?

With a VAXstation, it seems the graphics console and a serial console 
are functionally equivalent.  Is the ALPHA somehow different?  If so, 
why?

I like the memory self-test when a VAX powers up (with the histogram 
filling up); why does this not exist on ALPHA?


